  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7265114aa1e7f41ada19d74a427f9e13, type: 3}
  m_Name: ChannelsRangeCard
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: xpTURN.Feedback.Samples::xpTURN.Feedback.Samples.SampleCard
  Title: Channels & Range
  Try: Click the field (or move the marker and press Space) to set off a blast; pick
    Red, Blue or both to send on.
  See: "Every lamp has a receiver on the Red or the Blue channel \u2014 assets, not
    channel 0 that every default would hear \u2014 and a player gated by its distance
    from the blast: 5 m, a linear falloff into the intensity. The count is how many
    receivers took the send; a lamp past the gate still counts, its player refuses
    the play. A receiver's channel and range are set in the inspector. The lamps'
    colour punch adds to the colour (no flash limit). Before sends nothing."
  Controls: "Mouse \u2014 click \xB7 WASD \xB7 Arrows \xB7 Left stick \u2014 marker
    \xB7 Space \xB7 1 \xB7 Gamepad South \u2014 blast at the marker \xB7 Z \xB7 X
    \xB7 C \xB7 D-pad \u2014 Red \xB7 Blue \xB7 Both"
  SceneGuid: 3d6c82cc3fd67436694f2316a3bd7784
  SceneName: ChannelsRange
  RequiredType: xpTURN.Feedback.Samples.Advanced.ChannelsRangeLab, xpTURN.Feedback.Samples.Advanced.ChannelsRange
  RequiresText: 
  OpenInEditor: 0
